    body("Goal this week: Stop the scroll. Make her feel seen before she knows who Luxora is. Plant the belief that her problem is not her fault."),
    sp(40),

    ...postCard("DAY 1", "IDENTITY PAIN | REEL + CAPTION",
      "You didn't start your med spa to feel like this.\n\nNot like this.\n\nNot constantly busy but still unsure if next month is going to be okay.\nNot carrying everything alone while wondering if the business is actually working or just staying alive.\n\nYou started it because you knew you were capable of more.\nMore freedom.\nMore income.\nMore impact.\n\nBut somewhere along the way... it started to feel heavier than it should.\n\nThat's not a you problem.\n\nThat's a systems problem.\n\nAnd it's fixable.\n\nThis is for the med spa owner doing $500K to $3M who is done running on guesswork.\nLink in bio if you want to see where your revenue is actually leaking.",
      "HOOK: [look directly at camera, pause one second before speaking]\n\nBETHANY SAYS:\n\"You didn't start your med spa to feel like this.\"\n\n[pause two seconds]\n\n\"Not constantly busy but still unsure if next month is okay.\nNot carrying everything alone.\nNot wondering in the back of your mind if this is actually working or if you're just... keeping it alive.\"\n\n[slight lean forward]\n\n\"You started this because you knew you were capable of more.\"\n\n\"Somewhere along the way it got heavier than it should.\"\n\n\"That's not a you problem. That's a systems problem.\"\n\n[soft]\n\"And it's fixable.\"\n\n\"Link in bio.\"\n\n[cut]"
    ),

    ...postCard("DAY 2", "HIDDEN PAIN | CAPTION ONLY",
      "The hardest part about owning a med spa that no one talks about:\n\nYou can look completely successful from the outside.\nFull books. Great team. Visible in your community.\n\nAnd still feel completely unstable on the inside.\n\nStill not sure what next month looks like.\nStill the one your entire business depends on.\nStill exhausted in a way that a vacation doesn't fix.\n\nThat specific kind of tired has a name.\n\nIt's what happens when you've been growing a business without a real system underneath it.\n\nYou're not failing.\n\nYou're just carrying more than you should have to.\n\nThis is for the med spa owner who is done carrying it alone.\ntheluxoracollective.co"
    ),

    ...postCard("DAY 3", "SURVIVAL VS. SCALE | REEL + CAPTION",
      "If you're constantly chasing new leads, your business isn't scaling.\n\nIt's surviving.\n\nAnd deep down... you already know that.\n\nThe clinics doing $2M a year are not the ones with the biggest ad budgets.\nThey're the ones with a system behind every single appointment.\n\nLead comes in. It gets booked.\nBooking shows up. It gets converted.\nClient converts. She comes back.\n\nThat's not magic. That's a system.\n\nAnd until you have it, more leads just means more chaos.\n\nThis is for the med spa owner who is done surviving and ready to actually scale.",
      "HOOK: [no smile, direct to camera]\n\n\"If you're constantly chasing new leads...\"\n\n[pause]\n\n\"Your business isn't scaling.\"\n\n\"It's surviving.\"\n\n[pause, let it land]\n\n\"And deep down... you already know that.\"\n\n[tone shifts slightly, still calm]\n\n\"The clinics doing $2M a year are not the ones with the biggest ad budget.\"\n\n\"They're the ones with a system behind every single appointment.\"\n\n\"That's not luck. That's structure.\"\n\n[direct]\n\"When you're ready to build that, the link is in bio.\"\n\n[cut]"
    ),

    ...postCard("DAY 4", "HEAVY BUSINESS | CAPTION ONLY",
      "If your business feels heavy right now...\n\nThis is probably why.\n\nYou're the one who books the appointments.\nYou're the one who follows up when someone doesn't show.\nYou're the one who fills the gap when a staff member calls out.\nYou're the one who checks the numbers at the end of the day and tries to figure out where they went.\n\nYou're not running a business.\n\nYou're running a very expensive job where you are also the manager, the marketing team, and the closer.\n\nThat's not what you built this for.\n\nAnd it doesn't have to stay that way.\n\nThis is for the med spa owner doing $500K to $3M who knows something has to change.\nThe link in bio is the next step."
    ),

    ...postCard("DAY 5", "BUSY VS. PROFITABLE | REEL + CAPTION",
      "Being busy and being profitable are not the same thing.\n\nAnd nobody warns you about this when you open a med spa.\n\nYou can have a full schedule, a great team, loyal clients...\nAnd still not know what next month looks like.\n\nBusy means the chairs are filled.\nProfitable means the system underneath turns those chairs into reliable, recurring revenue.\n\nMost med spas have the first.\n\nVery few have built the second.\n\nThat is the gap. And that is what we fix.\n\nThis is for the owner who is ready to turn busy into something that actually compounds.",
      "HOOK: [relaxed, natural, like you're talking to a friend]\n\n\"Busy and profitable are not the same thing.\"\n\n[pause]\n\n\"Nobody tells you this when you open a med spa.\"\n\n\"You can have a full schedule. Great clients. A team you actually like.\"\n\n\"And still not know what next month looks like.\"\n\n[lean back slightly]\n\n\"Busy means the chairs are full.\"\n\n\"Profitable means the system underneath turns those chairs into something that actually compounds.\"\n\n[pause]\n\n\"Most clinics have the first. Very few have built the second.\"\n\n\"That's the gap. That's what we fix.\"\n\n[look at camera]\n\"Link in bio.\"\n\n[cut]"
